  'graham-road-repairs-tshwane-traffic-light-theft-2026-11-17',
  'Gauteng finishes Graham Road repairs, turns to traffic light theft',
  'Traffic', '2026-11-17', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/17/tshwane-motorists-get-smoother-rides-after-r14m-graham-road-upgrade/',
  'Gauteng''s roads department has finished resurfacing Pretoria''s Graham Road and is rolling out CCTV to curb traffic signal theft.',
  'Gauteng''s roads department has finished resurfacing Graham Road in Tshwane, ending months of complaints about potholes, broken traffic lights and slow-moving traffic around the Lynnwood Road and Struben Street area. The roughly 5km upgrade cost about R14 million and included milling the old surface, laying new asphalt and repainting road markings. Work started in late August and wrapped up by the end of October.

The same maintenance drive also completed work on Mogogelo Road and Makapan Road in Tshwane. Several other provincial routes were finished too, among them Cedar Road, Winnie Mandela Drive and the K46, along with the R28, R103, R548, R553 and D1132. Officials picked these sections because of how far they had deteriorated and the number of complaints from road users. Gauteng Roads and Transport MEC Kedibone Diale-Tlabela called the progress encouraging, adding that the department would now turn to other worn-out sections while still treating the poorest roads as a priority. A first round of appointing contractors to a new three-year maintenance panel is done, with that work due to begin in early December.

At the same time, the department is adding camera surveillance and other technology at busy intersections to tackle the theft and vandalism of traffic signals, which have knocked out lights for long stretches and driven up repair bills. Officials asked residents to report anyone tampering with traffic lights or other road infrastructure, and to avoid dumping rubbish on road reserves, which also damages the network.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/17/tshwane-motorists-get-smoother-rides-after-r14m-graham-road-upgrade/", "https://www.jacarandafm.com/news/news/gauteng-expands-road-maintenance-programme/"]',
  'agent'
);
